[0.119, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1;36mWait, the output says `1290731` and then `cr`. That means `mod` worked and gave the remainder \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m1290731. But let's verify: 82225043186179281 mod 6469193 = 1290731? We can double-check by \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36mmultiplying: 6469193 * quotient + 1290731 = 82225043186179281. We can compute quotient = \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m(82225043186179281 - 1290731) / 6469193. But the machine already gave the remainder. The problem \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36masks: \"Calculate the remainder when 82225043186179281 is divided by 6469193.\" The answer is 1290731.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36mWe should output it in \\boxed{}.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
