[0.071, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1mBut let's be cautious: the machine's `mod` might have given the correct remainder. The error for `/`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mwas because dividend over 10 digits, but `mod` apparently accepts larger dividends. The problem \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mstatement said \"/ and /mod: the dividend may have up to 10 digits (for a bigger number, n d mod \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mgives the remainder of any 20-digit n directly).\" It didn't say `mod` has the same limit. So `mod` \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mmight work for any numbers up to 20 digits. The output `1290731` seems plausible.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
